    {
      "title": "Sum the enclosed areas",
      "body": "<p>Use each allowed squared radius to calculate its disk area and recognise the resulting arithmetic progression.</p>",
      "recap": "Circle areas depend on squared radii, so an arithmetic progression in squared radii gives an arithmetic progression in disk areas.",
      "pitfall": "The question adds the enclosed areas even though the disks are nested.",
