  "solution": "<p><strong>1.</strong> Write <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x02265;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>. The tangent equation gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>&#x003C0;</mi></mrow></math> with integers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x02265;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>. Each value of u defines a circle centred at the origin with squared radius u, enclosing area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mi>u</mi></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>2.</strong> For a positive integer k, the condition <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>&#x003C0;</mi></mrow></math> permits precisely <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>&#x02026;</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>. The sum of the disk areas is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mo>&#x02211;</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007B;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007D;</mo></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>3.</strong> Equating to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>30</mn><msup><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math> gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>120</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>15</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>. The permitted positive integer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></math>. Answer D.</p><p><strong>4.</strong> The instruction sums the area enclosed by each circle separately; it does not ask for the area of their union or for annular bands.</p>"
